    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square given its perimeter, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the length of one side of the square:**\n   The perimeter \\( P \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   P = 4s\n   \\]\n   where \\( s \\) is the length of one side of the square. We know the perimeter is 32 feet, so we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   4s = 32\n   \\]\n   To find \\( s \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n   \\[\n   s = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the square:**\n   The area \\( A \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   A = s^2\n   \\]\n   Substituting the value of \\( s \\) that we found:\n   \\[\n   A = 8^2 = 64 \\text{ square feet}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{64}\\) square feet.",
