      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "A square has four equal sides. If the perimeter is 32 ft, we can find the length of one side by dividing the perimeter by 4.\n\nPerimeter = 32 ft\nSide length = Perimeter / 4\nSide length = 32 ft / 4\nSide length = 8 ft\n\nThe area of a square is found by squaring the length of one side. So, the area is:\n\nArea = Side length × Side length\nArea = 8 ft × 8 ft\nArea = 64 square feet\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\boxed{64} square feet.",
